# Where the JSON data bundles are served from.
#
# ONE value, read in two places — `src/lib/data.ts` (every runtime fetch) and
# `index.html` (the languages.json preload). They must agree, so they read the
# same variable rather than each hardcoding a path.
#
# The data does NOT live in the frontend. It is ~110MB of generated JSON whose
# source of truth is `data-prep`, not git, and a frontend directory is mirrored
# to the server with `rsync --delete`. Keeping the two apart is what makes a
# code deploy incapable of eating the data. See app.toml [data].
#
# In production `server.py` serves the data root at this path. In development
# `vite.config.ts` serves the SAME data root at the SAME path, so there is one
# set of bytes in one place and dev cannot drift from prod.
#
# Override to point at a CDN/S3 origin (an absolute URL works) via `.env.local`
# or a shell env var; both are gitignored / out of the repo.
VITE_DATA_BASE=/api/glossa/data
